\b\fs32 CarVibeDubai Development Milestone Plan\b0\fs24\par
\par
Prepared for: CarVibeDubai Management / Owner\par
Project: Car lead capture system, private admin dashboard, and CRM pipeline\par
Source basis: Signed CarVibeDubai proposal and CARVIBE_BUILD_PLAN.md\par
Timeline estimate: Up to 45 days / around 1.5 months from confirmed start date\par
Status: Milestone schedule prepared after the Developer Requirements Form\par
\par
\b\fs28 Short Message For Sir Nyash\b0\fs24\par
\par
Hi Sir Nyash,\par
\par
Thank you for completing the requirements form. I reviewed it together with our signed proposal, and I can now organize the project into clear development milestones.\par
\par
Based on the full approved scope, this is not just a basic landing page. The work includes the public CarVibeDubai website, the car valuation form, phone OTP verification, database setup, private admin dashboard, CRM pipeline, Gmail lead notifications, completed-sale tracking, profit calculation, and launch testing.\par
\par
For that reason, the safe timeline is around 1 and a half months, or up to 45 days from the confirmed start date. Some parts may be completed earlier, especially the public website design, but I do not want to rush the database, CRM, and admin logic because those parts need proper setup and testing.\par
\par
I will handle the project in 4 milestones:\par
\par
1. Public website and landing page.\par
2. Valuation form, OTP, and database foundation.\par
3. Private admin dashboard and CRM pipeline.\par
4. Notifications, settings, testing, launch preparation, and handover.\par
\par
The "Buy a Car" button will be prepared as agreed, but it will stay disabled by default until CarVibeDubai is ready to activate that future feature.\par
\par
The timeline can move faster if the logo, final contact details, Gmail, domain details, and feedback are provided early. But as a realistic expectation, please allow up to 45 days so the full system can be built properly.\par
\par
I will send progress updates as each milestone is completed.\par
\par
Thank you,\par
CarVibeDubai Development Team\par
\par
\b\fs28 Alignment With The Signed Proposal\b0\fs24\par
\par
This milestone plan follows the signed CarVibeDubai proposal and the technical build plan. It does not replace the signed proposal, change the agreed PHP 67,000 professional development fee, or expand the signed scope.\par
\par
The approved project focus is:\par
\par
\tab - Public CarVibeDubai website for car-seller lead capture.\par
\tab - Car submission form with Make, Model, Year, Mileage, and Condition.\par
\tab - Phone OTP verification through Twilio before submission.\par
\tab - Thank-you confirmation with no automatic price shown to the customer.\par
\tab - Private admin dashboard for authorized CarVibeDubai Management users.\par
\tab - CRM pipeline for tracking leads through sale or not-purchased stages.\par
\tab - Gmail notification when a new lead is submitted.\par
\tab - Completed-sale record with purchase price, final selling price, profit, and completion date.\par
\tab - Automatic 2% developer partnership-share calculation from completed-sale profit records.\par
\tab - Settings for contact details, Gmail address, pipeline stages, and future team member accounts.\par
\tab - Disabled "Buy a Car" button prepared for future activation.\par
\tab - Launch preparation, testing, handover, and 30-day technical warranty for original build defects.\par
\par
\b\fs28 Timeline Note\b0\fs24\par
\par
The 45-day timeline is a realistic estimate. Some parts may finish earlier if all details, assets, access, and feedback are ready on time. If the project is waiting for client information, approval, payment, domain access, Supabase access, Twilio setup, Gmail access, Meta Pixel details, or other required accounts, the timeline may extend accordingly.\par
\par
The plan should begin after:\par
\par
\tab - The finalized schedule is confirmed through the agreed written communication channel.\par
\tab - Required information and access are provided.\par
\tab - The first scheduled payment is received, based on the finalized payment milestone arrangement.\par
\par
\b\fs28 Milestone 1 - Public Website And Landing Page\b0\fs24\par
\par
Estimated schedule: Days 1 to 15\par
\par
Main goal: Prepare the customer-facing CarVibeDubai website so it looks premium, works well on mobile, and clearly leads visitors toward submitting their car details.\par
\par
Planned work:\par
\par
\tab - Build the public website using original code, not a pre-made template.\par
\tab - Prepare the premium black and gold landing page direction.\par
\tab - Add the main headline, supporting message, and call-to-action.\par
\tab - Prepare the navigation for the main sections.\par
\tab - Add the How It Works section.\par
\tab - Add the valuation entry area for customers.\par
\tab - Add the floating WhatsApp chat and call access.\par
\tab - Prepare the disabled "Buy a Car" button as agreed.\par
\tab - Add the contact section and footer, including the approved developer credit line.\par
\tab - Make the page responsive for phones, tablets, and desktop screens.\par
\tab - Review and adjust wording, spacing, and layout based on feedback.\par
\par
Expected result by the end of this milestone:\par
\par
\tab - A premium public website direction is ready for review.\par
\tab - Customers can understand what CarVibeDubai offers and where to submit their car details.\par
\tab - The public page is mobile-friendly and aligned with the signed black/gold direction.\par
\tab - Remaining revisions should mostly be wording, images, spacing, or brand-detail adjustments.\par
\par
Client input needed:\par
\par
\tab - Final logo file.\par
\tab - Final brand name spelling.\par
\tab - Preferred headline and short message.\par
\tab - WhatsApp number, call number, and public contact details.\par
\tab - Approval of footer credit wording.\par
\tab - Any final design reference or Canva notes.\par
\par
\b\fs28 Milestone 2 - Valuation Form, OTP, And Database Foundation\b0\fs24\par
\par
Estimated schedule: Days 16 to 25\par
\par
Main goal: Prepare the customer submission flow so real leads can be validated, verified, and stored properly.\par
\par
Planned work:\par
